{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@preconcurrency"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"map"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transformed"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"transform"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@escaping","kind":"attribute"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncSequence\/Element","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp","text":"Transformed"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceV","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncThrowingMapSequence","text":"AsyncThrowingMapSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp","text":"Transformed"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"transform","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A mapping closure. ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accepts an element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of this sequence as its parameter and returns a transformed value of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same or of a different type. ","type":"text"},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can also throw an error, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends the transformed sequence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An asynchronous sequence that contains, in order, the elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produced by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"type":"text","text":" closure."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method to transform every element received from a base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous sequence. Typically, you use this to transform from one type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of element to another."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this example, an asynchronous sequence called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values from ","type":"text"},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"5","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The closure provided to the "},{"code":"map(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"takes each "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and looks up a corresponding "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"romanNumeralDict","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dictionary. This means the outer ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await in","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"iterates over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" instances instead of the underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces. Also, the dictionary doesn’t provide a key for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4"},{"type":"text","text":", and the closure throws an error for any key it can’t look up, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receiving this value from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" ends the modified sequence with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let romanNumeralDict: [Int: String] =","    [1: \"I\", 2: \"II\", 3: \"III\", 5: \"V\"]","","do {","    let stream = Counter(howHigh: 5)","        .map { (value) throws -> String in","            guard let roman = romanNumeralDict[value] else {","                throw MyError()","            }","            return roman","        }","    for try await numeral in stream {","        print(numeral, terminator: \" \")","    }","} catch {","    print(\"Error: \\(error)\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"I II III Error: MyError() \""]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates an asynchronous sequence that maps the given error-throwing","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure over the asynchronous sequence’s elements."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swift","relatedModules":[]}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"map"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transformed"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind"